{
  "info": {
    "name": "ERP Inventory Management",
    "description": "Full end-to-end flow for the ERP Inventory Management API (Spring Boot + JWT + PostgreSQL).\n\nRun the requests top to bottom (or use the Collection Runner). Test scripts automatically capture the JWT tokens and every created resource id into collection variables, so later requests just work.\n\nFlow order:\n1. Auth -> Login (captures accessToken + refreshToken)\n2. Master Data -> create Category, Supplier, Warehouse, Customer, Product\n3. Purchase Orders -> create + complete (stock goes IN)\n4. Inventory -> adjust / inspect stock and movements\n5. Sales Orders -> create (stock goes OUT, auto-completed) + cancel (stock restored)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Attach the captured JWT to every request except the auth endpoints and the",
          "// deliberate 'no token' check. Keeps the collection working in Newman too,",
          "// which does not always apply collection-level bearer auth to child requests.",
          "var url = (pm.request.url && pm.request.url.toString()) || '';",
          "var name = (pm.info && pm.info.requestName) || '';",
          "var token = pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken');",
          "var skip = url.indexOf('/api/auth/') !== -1 || name.indexOf('Unauthorized') !== -1;",
          "if (token && !skip) {",
          "  pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Authorization', value: 'Bearer ' + token });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
